{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 18, :comments ["<b>For Your salvation I hope, O YHWH.</b> There was none among all the judges of Israel who fell into the hand of his enemies besides Samson — he is this serpent, as it is written (Judges 2:18), 'And YHWH was with the judge and saved them from the hand of their enemies all the days of the judge.' And he was the last of the judges, for Samuel was a prophet and did not wage war for them, and in his days the kings reigned. And when the prophet saw that the salvation of Samson had been cut off, he said, 'For Your salvation I hope, O YHWH' — not for the salvation of a serpent and a viper, for in You do I hope for salvation, not in a judge, for Your salvation is an everlasting salvation.'"], :book :genesis, :voice :ramban, :lang :en, :chapter 49, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T03:47:01.553329468Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}